 ### Verification
 
 All 179 tests across the 14 requested Vitest files passed in individual runs at `nice -n 19`. The no-emit TypeScript check (`tsc -b`), Oxlint on the edited TypeScript files, and the Git whitespace check passed. Cloud CI timings and new browser stills remain unverified.
+
+## Round 18 (N3k)
+
+### 1. Drawn grid
+
+The Jerusalem broken-low fixture draws Sc at **144 × 73**. The 375 CSS px fixture spans 250°, giving **1.7483° and 2.6224 CSS px per horizontal texel interval**. Elevation spacing is nonuniform, from **0.00013° to 5.943°** in this fixture. A 24-column grid would give 16.30 CSS px per horizontal interval in the same view. The reported 9 px steps therefore do not identify the broad grid. A visible step can span several columns and the more widely spaced elevation rows.
+
+### 2. Opacity coverage
+
+The resolved Sc/Ac source now uses `1 − mean(exp(−τ × slant))` over the projected deck texel, with equal-area radial strata and deterministic azimuth midpoints. Adjacent ray midpoints bound each footprint. The sampler uses 2 × 2 taps for differing neighbours above one alpha byte and 3 × 3 at differences above 0.5. It reads the same instantaneous `resolvedTauAt` kernel as the previous cellular point sample. N3j had already removed the separate N3f edge contrast from this opacity path. The unresolved source and direct solar chord retain their previous treatment.
+
+### 3. Tests
+
+- **Fractional edges failed.** Of 1,723 output texels with a four-connected neighbour more than 0.5 away in alpha, **43.53%** were in 0.15–0.85. Point sampling gives 17.28%. The 16 × 16 reference integrated every resolved texel over the same footprint and gave 44.71%, also below 60%. The reference suggests that refining the quadrature alone will leave the gate unmet. A wider footprint spanning the adjacent ray centres was also tried and rejected after it missed the gate.
+- The mean texel alpha changed by **+0.0000352**. Weighting by screen area gives **−0.002964**. Both pass the ±0.02 gate.
+- The motion-compensated test pulls each quadrature ray back by the wind and sums the Beer–Lambert slope bounds over the same footprint. The largest p99 was **0.07778** against 0.15. The pointwise slope and midnight gates passed. The N3j seam, tone and aspect checks also passed.
+
+### 4. Performance
+
+Median local timings in milliseconds from the existing performance fixture:
+
+| Panorama | Reused increment | Total raster | Raster extension | N3j gate total | Cold increment |
+| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |
+| Jerusalem | −0.137 | 0.987 | 0.621 | 0.484 | 20.646 |
+| Haifa | 0.014 | 1.031 | 0.620 | 0.634 | 19.762 |
+| Tiberias | 0.035 | 0.899 | 0.550 | 0.585 | 19.060 |
+
+The N3j 1.5 ms gate passed on all three panoramas.
+
+### Cold snapshot cost
+
+The cold path still exceeds the 4 ms target. A local CPU-profiled replay using N3j's point-sample model measured 7.22 ms in Jerusalem, 7.68 ms in Haifa and 9.15 ms in Tiberias. Sheet grid evaluation was the largest sampled cost there. Raster construction separately measured about 1 ms. The profile sampled the clump and texture functions less often than the sheet build.
+
+With coverage, the grid and footprint evaluation also dominated. Precomputing directions and radii removed trigonometry and square roots from the per-edge loop. Each cold snapshot still evaluates the 144 × 73 grid for each cellular sheet and makes extra field and transmission evaluations at the edges. The best measured local range for this implementation was 19.06–20.65 ms of cold overhead. CI-equivalent timings and a 16 ms mid-phone frame remain unverified.
+
+### Verification
+
+181 of 182 tests passed across 15 explicit Vitest file runs at `nice -n 19`, including the painter unit file. The Jerusalem fractional-edge assertion was the sole failure. TypeScript build-mode checking with no emit, Oxlint on the edited TypeScript files, and Git's whitespace check passed. The temporary diagnostic files were removed. Cloud CI, full builds and browser stills were skipped locally.
